Welcome to the very first design
competition

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.300
where once and for all
we will decide who is better.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:11.678
The architects or the AIs.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.306
Each team will be tested on their design
skills,

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:18.727
rendering skills,
and the ability to describe their work.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:22.605
The winner will be unanimously decided
by our Discord

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:32.198
server, Archibeans.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:32.949
Oh, hey, guys.

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:35.201
Welcome.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:40.999
And to make sure human architects
can perform at their best,

00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:47.422
HP provided the Z8 Fury G5
a powerful workstation equipped with 56

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:51.092
cores, 128 gigabytes of RAM 4 RTX

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:55.055
A6000 that will speed up
any human made process.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:57.432
Thank you
HP for sponsoring this competition.

00:00:57.474 --> 00:00:58.892
Much appreciated.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.019
The competition's pull
from different phases

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:04.647
of the design process
and will lead to the design of a 280

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:07.901
square meter house on a hill.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:09.903
Design a floor

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.490
plan for a 280 square meter house
on a sloped terrain

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:18.995
The site is approximately 3000 square
meters and approximately 20 degree angle.

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:22.207
The house must have three bedrooms
and a pool

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.418
and take advantage of the view
overlooking the hill.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.670
So how many square feet was that?

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.881
Sorry. It's 280 square meters.

00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:31.966
What was the angle of the slope?

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:35.220
20 degree slope.

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:41.392
As soon as they said plan,
I knew we had the advantage.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.313
Our strategy was to simultaneously develop
three different ideas

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:48.983
since we knew the next challenge
was to create a compelling rendering.

00:01:49.192 --> 00:01:52.237
We will pick an option
that leads to the most compelling form

00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:56.741
a challenge within a challenge.

00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:59.619
Option one The cantilevered

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:03.790
with the bedrooms on the bottom volume
and the kitchen and living spaces on top.

00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:08.169
Both volumes cantilever
over the slope with minimal interruption

00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:09.462
to the landscape.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.674
The intersection of the two volumes create
a light filled double

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:15.718
storey atrium that connects the different
spaces of the house.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.305
Option two The fan.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:23.351
Like the name, suggests, this option
maximizes the width of the site.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.230
Like a fan and creates
wide open views onto the hill.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.442
We've got our bedrooms which are angled
towards the sun and living

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:35.238
and kitchen spaces, all in one story
with a pool right in the center.

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.615
Option three The Cascade.

00:02:37.615 --> 00:02:39.784
This option follows the landscape.

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:43.872
Each volume gets a unique view
and the interior spaces overlook

00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:46.958
onto each other, creating a connection
between different floors.

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:51.254
Each of the bedrooms get direct
exterior access with a pool jutting out

00:02:51.254 --> 00:03:05.518
next to the living spaces.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.108
That's actually pretty good.

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:16.571
All right.

00:03:16.571 --> 00:03:17.906
We need to pick a plan.

00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:18.489
Okay.

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:22.035
Well, I really like how your sits
in the topography and yours.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:25.413
Look. Absolutely.
We need to pick one plan.

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:34.297
Guys, let's just pick
something that looks good in the renders.

00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:42.722
what the hell?

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.598
Oh, wow.

00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:46.309
That's a crack.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.896
Yo can you try to model this?

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.653
Yeah. Hmm.

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:58.404
Yeah, right there.

00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:00.198
It's kind of cool.

00:04:00.198 --> 00:04:01.532
Challenge number two.

00:04:01.532 --> 00:04:05.203
Develop The floor plans
into two compelling conceptual renderings

00:04:05.203 --> 00:04:06.996
that tell the story of your building.

00:04:06.996 --> 00:04:10.750
Take into consideration
the unique characteristics of the site.

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:16.005
The word compelling
is the key to this challenge.

00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:16.881
All right, team.

00:04:16.881 --> 00:04:18.591
So what's the game plan?

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.802
So someone needs to populate the site.

00:04:20.802 --> 00:04:22.971
Someone need to do the building .
The pool.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.766
That's going to be our money shot
No, they're not the pool.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:30.353
Please, not the pool Not the pool.

00:04:31.854 --> 00:04:34.148
All right, I'll take the landscape.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.192
Okay. I'll take the building.

00:04:36.192 --> 00:04:51.708
So, Trushit you take the pool.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.043
Okay, That's really creepy.

00:04:54.085 --> 00:04:56.713
The setting often makes
or breaks a render.

00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:58.798
And because we didn't
have a huge amount of time

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.592
to spend in Photoshop,
nailing down the context.

00:05:01.592 --> 00:05:04.012
Right in our rendering
software was essential.

00:05:04.095 --> 00:05:07.181
Because of this,
we decided to use D5, which has

00:05:07.223 --> 00:05:08.975
thousands of high quality models.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.935
You can easily plop into your model.

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:12.937
You can see the changes in real time.

00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:17.317
It's super intuitive and you can render
complex scenes without a problem.

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:20.320
So you can really speed up
the visualization process.

00:05:20.528 --> 00:05:21.612
We laid down the grass

00:05:21.612 --> 00:05:25.742
and combined different types of vegetation
that we felt worked in this landscape.

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.661
We wanted to bring focus
to the crevice at the center.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.163
So the flanking volumes on

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:34.000
either sides should be quieter,
a bit more integrated with the site.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.129
We decided to use wood siding
with the soffit and balcony in dark metal.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.881
After playing around
with a bunch of different

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:43.176
material options,
we landed on concrete for the mass wall.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.386
The pool is the money shot.

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:47.430
The entry experience should be exquisite.

00:05:47.638 --> 00:05:51.142
With the refraction of the pool
showering you as you enter the house.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.145
Equally important is the view
from the top, with the infinity

00:05:54.145 --> 00:06:09.410
pool overlooking the hill.

00:06:12.246 --> 00:06:12.705
Okay.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:15.124
Are you guys ready?

00:06:17.585 --> 00:06:18.252
All right, quick,

00:06:18.252 --> 00:06:27.428
let's set up the views.

00:06:28.429 --> 00:06:35.978
Nice, guys.

00:06:36.604 --> 00:06:46.697
Look,

00:06:46.697 --> 00:06:49.617
DAMN.

